{
  "_doc": [
    "What 'valid' means in this repository, in one place. scripts/lint.py enforces",
    "it, scripts/doctor.py reports it, the doctor skill reads it, and a",
    "person can read it too. Change a convention here and in the folder README",
    "that explains it, in the same proposal. Keys starting with _ are comments."
  ],
  "stale_after_days": 90,
  "repo": {
    "_doc": "Whether the repository is private. Ships true, because transcripts and strategy belong in a private repository; set it to match yours (/setup asks). private: true turns the PII finding into an info line (data/README.md says private repos may hold names; log that decision); scripts/doctor.py --github warns when this disagrees with GitHub.",
    "private": true
  },
  "review": {
    "_doc": "self_merge: true means the author's own merge counts as the approval on a needs-review proposal, for a repository with one maintainer. Ships false: a team needs someone other than the author to approve. /setup asks how many people merge and sets it. The gate still classifies and labels, the health check must still be green, and a person still reads the diff and clicks merge. Set it back to false the day a second person joins (docs/workflow.md). The gate runs from main, so a change here takes effect once it lands there. The Actions variable REVIEW_SELF_MERGE=true has the same effect without changing this file; the template repository itself uses that.",
    "self_merge": false
  },
